=== READING GUIDE ===
  C1+C2 strong, C3 flat  -> that speaker's RECORDING SESSION. Fix is data-side or
                            per-speaker; it will not generalise to Test.
  C1+C2 strong, C3 strong-> a FRONT-END gap that also drives the corpus empties.
                            Highest value: one fix, two problems.
  C1+C2 flat             -> the audio is in-family; the failure is in the MODEL for
                            this talker. No front-end fix exists. Needs training data.
  C4 strong              -> within this speaker, the empties are acoustically distinct
                            -> a per-utterance trigger exists, not a per-speaker one.

